<title>FRANCE: Hungary orders Matra-BAe anti-aircarft missiles.</title>
<headline>Hungary orders Matra-BAe anti-aircarft missiles.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's ministry of defence signed with Matra BAe Dynamics on April 2 an order for &quot;about $100 million&quot; for Mistral anti-aircraft missiles, Groupe Lagardere said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The contract includes Atlas firing units and Mistral Coordination Posts to synchronise multiple missile firings, Lagardere said in a statement.</p>
<p>Matra BAe is a joint unit of Lagardere and British Aerospace Plc that has been operational since November 1, 1996.</p>
<p>Lagardere said Hungary was the 21st country to order the Mistral.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
